0.1.0 (2026-11-25)
  * First build (queue row 68): System Settings' Colour Vision page beside Accessibility, one choice (none, protan, deutan,
    tritan, monochromacy) and a box for the terminals. It sets KWin's colour correction through the keys KDE's Accessibility
    page uses, the colour-vision variant of the person's colour scheme, Konsole's default profile (a profile of ours whose
    parent is the person's), nano's colours when the person has no nano settings file, and the line the text console's
    login reads. The person's own files are kept and their colours come back exactly at None; what could not be set is said
    on the page. The maps are the accessibility study's of 2026-10-14 (section 1.3), corrected per kind by measurement.
